  {
    "kp_id": "natural-exponential-function/kp1",
    "kind": "template",
    "status": "pending",
    "arguments": {
      "statement": "Two plans both split nominal annual $100\\%$ growth equally. The first compounds {a} times per year; the second compounds {b} times. Find the ratio of the first annual multiplier to the second, as an exact fraction.",
      "answer_expr": "compounding(a)/compounding(b)",
      "solution_sketch": "With $n$ equal updates, each factor is $1+1/n$ and the annual factor is $(1+1/n)^n$. Evaluate that power for $n={a}$ and $n={b}$, then divide the first annual factor by the second.",
      "hints": [
        "How many times is the per-update factor multiplied by itself in each plan?"
      ],
      "params": {
        "a": {
          "kind": "choice",
          "values": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        "b": {
          "kind": "choice",
          "values": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        }
      },
      "constraints": [
        {
          "op": "ne",
          "left": "a",
          "right": "b"
        }
      ],
      "samples": [
        {
          "params": {
            "a": 1,
            "b": 2
          },
          "expected": "8/9"
        },
